{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"e7ec7b7b-017a-4621-8193-207115a84d7f","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Light meets a boundary between air and glass. Measure the incoming angle from the dashed normal, not from the surface.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Snell's law"},{"op":"figure","id":"boundary","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-3.2,3.2],"y":[-3.4,3.8],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"surface","from":[-3,0],"to":[3,0]},{"kind":"point","id":"entry","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"segment","id":"normal","from":[0,-3.1],"to":[0,3.5],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[2,2.9],"text":"air: n₁ = 1"},{"kind":"text","at":[-1.6,-2.8],"text":"glass: n₂ = 1.5"},{"kind":"segment","id":"incident","from":[-1.8,3.1177],"to":{"at":"entry"},"arrow":true},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"entry"},"from":[0,3],"to":[-1.8,3.1177],"r":0.22,"label":"30°"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"given","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"n_1=1,\\quad n_2=1.5,\\quad \\theta_1=30^\\circ"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"e7ec7b7b-017a-4621-8193-207115a84d7f","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Snell's law connects the two angles. Entering higher-index glass, light bends toward the normal, so its refracted angle is smaller.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"transmit","on":"boundary","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"refracted","from":{"at":"entry"},"to":[1,-2.8284],"arrow":true},{"kind":"angle","at":{"at":"entry"},"from":[0,-3],"to":[1,-2.8284],"r":0.27,"label":"θ₂"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"snell","anchor":{"el":"given","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"n_1\\sin\\theta_1=n_2\\sin\\theta_2"},{"op":"equation","id":"substitute","anchor":{"el":"snell","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\sin\\theta_2=\\frac{1}{1.5}\\sin30^\\circ=\\frac13"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"e7ec7b7b-017a-4621-8193-207115a84d7f","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s3"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"e7ec7b7b-017a-4621-8193-207115a84d7f","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Taking inverse sine gives about nineteen point five degrees. The smaller angle confirms bending toward the normal; higher index also means slower light.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"substitute","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"\\theta_2=\\sin^{-1}(1/3)\\approx19.5^\\circ"},{"op":"figure","id":"annotate","on":"boundary","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[1.7,-1.5],"text":"19.5°"},{"kind":"text","at":[-1.7,-1.2],"text":"slower light"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
